  "body": "<feed xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom\"><entry>\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t\t<name>Lauren Feiner</name>\n\t\t\t</author>\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t\t<name>Hayden Field</name>\n\t\t\t</author>\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t<title type=\"html\"><![CDATA[Trump engineered a risky comeback for Jensen Huang]]></title>\n\t\t\t<link rel=\"alternate\" type=\"text/html\" href=\"https://www.theverge.com/ai-artificial-intelligence/1040652/jensen-huang-nvidia-trump-reinstated\" />\n\t\t\t<id>https://www.theverge.com/?p=1040652</id>\n\t\t\t<updated>2026-11-23T17:34:20-05:00</updated>\n\t\t\t<published>2026-11-23T17:25:12-05:00</published>\n\t\t\t<category scheme=\"https://www.theverge.com\" term=\"AI\" /><category scheme=\"https://www.theverge.com\" term=\"Analysis\" /><category scheme=\"https://www.theverge.com\" term=\"Nvidia\" /><category scheme=\"https://www.theverge.com\" term=\"Policy\" /><category scheme=\"https://www.theverge.com\" term=\"Politics\" /><category scheme=\"https://www.theverge.com\" term=\"Report\" /><category scheme=\"https://www.theverge.com\" term=\"Tech\" />\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<summary type=\"html\"><![CDATA[After Nvidia's board accepted Jensen Huang's resignation as CEO, following reports that Huang had an affair with an alleged Chinese spy, President Donald Trump, too, appeared to submit to the new reality. Appearing on Stephen A. Smith's radio show shortly after the news came out, Trump said that Huang would \"end up on his feet.\" [&#8230;]]]></summary>\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<content type=\"html\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<![CDATA[\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\n<figure>\n\n<img alt=\"\" data-caption=\"\" data-portal-copyright=\"Image: Kevin Dietsch/Getty Images\" data-has-syndication-rights=\"1\" src=\"https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/11/gettyimages-2297774940.jpg?quality=90&#038;strip=all&#038;crop=0,0,100,100\" />\n\t<figcaption>\n\t\t</figcaption>\n</figure>\n<p class=\"has-drop-cap wp-block-paragraph\">After Nvidia's board <a href=\"https://www.theverge.com/ai-artificial-intelligence/1031689/jensen-huang-nvidia-ceo-resigns\">accepted Jensen Huang's resignation as CEO</a>, following reports that Huang had an affair with an alleged Chinese spy, President Donald Trump, too, appeared to submit to the new reality. Appearing on <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Q2xPvRnU4oI\">Stephen A. Smith's radio show</a> shortly after the news came out, Trump said that Huang would \"end up on his feet.\"</p>\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">\"You know the expression, anybody can be replaced,\" Trump said, <a href=\"https://www.theverge.com/tech/1032774/president-donald-trump-tim-cook-nvidia-jensen-huang\">floating Apple's ex-CEO Tim Cook</a> as a potential CEO candidate.</p>\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">It didn't take long for Trump to begin softening his approach, making it clear he'd welcome Huang back into the role of CEO even if Nvidia's own board wasn't ready to do so. Behind the scen …</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.theverge.com/ai-artificial-intelligence/1040652/jensen-huang-nvidia-trump-reinstated\">Read the full story at The Verge.</a></p>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t]]>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</content>\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t</entry></feed>"
}